        <zone h='21269' id='18' type-v2='text' w='58419' x='1388' y='69330'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Key Insights</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>• Overall failure rate is </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>3.39%</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>.&#10;• </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>L-type</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'> products have the highest failure rate (</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>3.92%</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>).
• Failed machines have significantly higher average tool wear (</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>143.78 min</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>) than non-failed machines (</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>106.69 min</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='11'>).
• Preventive maintenance based on tool wear could help reduce machine failures.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
